      "title": "New major risk - Financial position",
      "body": "The company's interest payments are not well covered by earnings. Net interest cover: 2.2x This is considered a major risk. If the company is unable to fund interest repayments on its debt through profits, it may be forced into reducing its debt burden through selling assets, undertaking a potentially costly capital raising or even into bankruptcy in the worst case scenario. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Major Risks Interest payments are not well covered by earnings (2.2x net interest cover). High level of non-cash earnings (70% accrual ratio). Minor Risks Revenue is less than US$5m (₹278m revenue, or US$2.9m). Market cap is less than US$100m (₹2.67b market cap, or US$28.0m).",
